|note_res_ELGS=[[Arsenal F.C.|Arsenal]] qualified for the [[2017–18 UEFA Europa League#Group stage|Europa League group stage]] by winning the [[2016–17 FA Cup]]. As they had also qualified there by the virtue of their league position (5th), this spot was passed to the next-highest ranked team (6th), [[Manchester United F.C.|Manchester United]].

|note_res_ELTH=[[Manchester United F.C.|Manchester United]] qualified for the [[2017–18 UEFA Champions League#Group stage|Champions League group stage]] by winning the [[2016–17 UEFA Europa League]]. Based on their league position (6th), they would have received the spot above to enter the [[2017–18 UEFA Europa League#Group stage|Europa League group stage]]. This spot was vacated without replacement as per UEFA regulations.

|note_res_EL3Q=[[Manchester United F.C.|Manchester United]], winners of the [[2016–17 EFL Cup]], initially attained a spot in the [[2017–18 UEFA Europa League#Third qualifying round|Europa League third qualifying round]]. That was passed to the next-highest ranked team in the league not already qualified for UEFA competitions (7th-placed [[Everton F.C.|Everton]]).

